  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "The number of atomic orbitals from the following having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> radial nodes is<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The number of radial nodes for an orbital with principal quantum number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> and azimuthal quantum number<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> is given by the expression:</p><p>Number of radial nodes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Using this expression, we can determine the number of radial nodes for each of the given atomic orbitals:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Therefore, the atomic orbitals with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> radial nodes are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>",
